    "title": "CMS Executive Cabinet member charged with DWI after police say he blew a .11 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By DJ Beal ,\n1 days ago CHARLOTTE, N.C. – A Charlotte-Mecklenburg Schools employee has been arrested after showing signs of impairment while operating a vehicle. Stephen Esposito, 46, was stopped during a safety checkpoint on Idlewild Road near Interstate 485. According to the arrest record, Esposito smelled strongly of alcohol and had red glassy eyes when stopped. Esposito admitted to consuming alcohol and performed poorly on the standardized field sobriety test. Read full article",
